# Peach Blueberry Crisp / Cobbler

Based on [https://www.mccormick.com/recipes/…](https://www.mccormick.com/recipes/dessert/peach-blueberry-crisp?amp=1) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20221204215314/https://www.mccormick.com/recipes/dessert/peach-blueberry-crisp?amp=1))

{ rating="2" image="peach_blueberry_crisp.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Peach Blueberry Filling

- [ ] 4 cups [peaches]{ ing="peaches" }, peeled and sliced
- [ ] 1 cup [blueberries]{ ing="blueberries" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Pure Vanilla Extract]{ ing="pure-vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [Cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" }, Ground

### Streusel Topping

- [ ] 1/2 cup [flour]{ ing="flour" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup [quick-cooking oats]{ ing="quick-cooking-oats" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup firmly packed [light brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" }, Ground
- [ ] 6 Tbsp [cold butter]{ ing="cold-butter" }, cut into chunks

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350
1. For the Peach-Blueberry Filling, toss fruit with [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" } and vanilla in large bowl
1. Mix [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" } and 2 teaspoons [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" } in small bowl then sprinkle over fruit and toss to coat well
1. Spoon the fruit into a lightly greased 11” x 7” baking dish (or smaller dishes if decreasing cook time)
1. For the Streusel Topping, mix [flour]{ ing="flour" }, [oats]{ ing="quick-cooking-oats" }, [brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }, and 1 tsp [cinnamon]{ ing="cinnamon" } in medium bowl
1. Cut in [butter]{ ing="cold-butter" } with 2 knives until coarse crumbs form. Sprinkle evenly over fruit (in the baking dish)
1. Bake 40 to 45 minutes or until fruit is tender and topping is golden brown. Serve warm with ice cream or whipped cream!
